Both pieces look good. The positional feature is almost perfectly linear at the block-5 input: held-out reply "answer"/"is" positions score 1.00 ± 0.03, every other token about 0 ± 0.05 (the user's own "is"/"answer" 0.04 ± 0.13). And the geometry explains the head: H1's query is already strongly bos-aligned (bos score +33), and the guess beats bos by only ~2 nats when present. Because the query is RMS-normalised, adding a bos-key-aligned component to it rotates it toward the bos key, and in the limit every other key loses. So the edit is W_q[head] += c · b̂ · aᵀ, with a the positional probe and b̂ the bos-key direction in that head's pre-norm query space. I now test offline which heads and what strength are needed: attention from the reply "answer"/"is" to the user's post-question tokens in T (odd facts) and D, and drift of the no-guess patterns at reply positions and elsewhere.

```python
