The leak hypothesis is confirmed. The probes were fit only on training-type sentences, and on new question types they give scores far from zero on ordinary question tokens. At block 7 the standard deviation is 0.31 with values up to +1.7 ("Monday", "Red", "hour", "day") and down to −1.7 ("legs", "does", "spider"); blocks 9 and 10 have sd 0.17 and 0.15 with peaks near 1 on "a", "have", "largest". A positive score pushes a question token's key away from all heads (hidden like a guess), and a negative score makes it bos-like, so it attracts attention. Either way the question-reading heads at the answer position are disturbed, which explains why "How many hours/legs…" broke.

