The data pass returned hidden states for 239 texts: 110 guess prompts in 12 phrasings on new fact kinds, and 129 no-guess messages. Now I will parse it, locating each guess token span by character offsets and checking the tokenization against the pass metadata. Before refitting anything, I will score the currently installed probes (blocks 7, 9, 10, 11, 12) on this new data. That tells me how well the current edit actually recognises guesses of new kinds in new phrasings (the guess-token score should be near 1) and how much it leaks on the new no-guess messages. If the installed probes detect new-kind guesses poorly or leak widely here, that quantifies the room for improvement and motivates the refit.

