On no-guess texts the refit key edits (using fold probes that never saw the text's kind) disturb reply-position attention less than the old ones at blocks 7, 9 and 10 at the same strength: mean total variation per head drops by roughly a third to a half, and worst cases from 0.79 to 0.54 at block 7 and from 0.76 to 0.37 at block 9. At blocks 11 and 12 the disturbance is about the same as before. Halving the strength halves the disturbance everywhere.

So the question is how much strength is needed to keep attention off the guess. I will now compute the other half of the dose-response on prompts with a guess: the attention mass the heads at the reply's answer position put on the guess tokens, for β from 0 to 1.5, using dev guess prompts in phrasings T, A (pass 16) and B, C (pass 2), with the installed query edits held fixed. If β = 0.5 already removes most of the guess attention, I can install the refit probes at half strength and cut no-guess disturbance by about 3–4× relative to the current edit.

